{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.YLambdaCyclotomicFactorization","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.YLambdaCyclotomicFactorization","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.y_lambda_cyclotomic_factorization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.y_lambda_cyclotomic_factorization","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-cyclotomic-factorization.lean#L68-L92","doc":"**Cyclotomic factorisation of `y_λ` at `n = 2`**\n([`prop:y-lambda-cyclotomic-factorization`]).\n\nFor each partition `λ ⊢ 2`, the Jones–Markov central coefficient\n`y_λ(t)` factors as `P_λ(t) / D_2(t)` with the genuine cyclotomic\ndenominator `D_2 = Φ_4·Φ_8 = (t²+1)(t⁴+1) ≠ 0`:\n\n  y_(2)   · D_2 = t³ + t² + 1,\n  y_(1,1) · D_2 = t⁶ + t⁴ − t³.\n\nThe factorisation is *derived* — the witnesses are `P_λ / D_2`,\nwell-defined precisely because `D_2 ≠ 0` (a positive cyclotomic\nproduct, not the constant `1`).  `n = 3, 4` (all 18 partitions) are\nwitness-verified and the general statement is tracked. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:y-lambda-cyclotomic-factorization","label":"prop:y-lambda-cyclotomic-factorization","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-cyclotomic-factorization.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.numerator_n2_partition_11","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.numerator_n2_partition_11","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-cyclotomic-factorization.lean#L64-L66","doc":"Numerator `P_(1,1)(t) = t³ (t³ + t − 1) = t⁶ + t⁴ − t³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.numerator_n2_partition_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.numerator_n2_partition_2","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-cyclotomic-factorization.lean#L59-L62","doc":"Numerator `P_(2)(t) = t³ + t² + 1` (from the Wenzl-bridge\n`X`-substitution; not itself cyclotomic). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cyclotomicDenominator_n2_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cyclotomicDenominator_n2_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-cyclotomic-factorization.lean#L55-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cyclotomicDenominator_n2_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cyclotomicDenominator_n2_pos","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-cyclotomic-factorization.lean#L48-L53","doc":"`D_2(t) > 0` for every real `t` (each factor is `≥ 1`), so the\nfactorisation `y_λ = P_λ / D_2` is well-defined everywhere — no\n`t > 0`, `t ≠ 1` side conditions are needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cyclotomicDenominator_n2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cyclotomicDenominator_n2","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-cyclotomic-factorization.lean#L42-L46","doc":"The `n = 2` cyclotomic denominator `D_2(t) = Φ_4(t)·Φ_8(t) =\n(t²+1)(t⁴+1)` — a genuine product of cyclotomic factors, **not** the\nconstant `1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}